# promise: #106
# What an extension sets on its toolbar action while it runs (chrome.action.setBadgeText, setTitle) reaches
# Cra's buttons: Chromium's Extensions.actionUpdated, through the browser's DevTools pipe. The icons never
# changed (#106). The fixture sets its badge and title when a page asks it to.
budget rss=800 stalls50=10
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/TabsCreateExtension
relaunch
cra://debug?actionState=${TABS_CREATE_EXTENSION_ID}
expect-log action state \S+: title=Cra Tabs Create Fixture badge= icon=manifest
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=badge
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 3
cra://debug?actionState=${TABS_CREATE_EXTENSION_ID}
expect-log action state \S+: title=Seven badge=7 icon=manifest
